        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1951-03-13/pdf/FR-1951-03-13.pdf"
      },
      "text": "1 . So much of the health services and \nspecial weapons defense functions now  \nbeing performed by the Health Re­\nsources Office of the National Security  \nResources Board as relates to civil de­\nfense is hereby transferred to the Fed­\neral Civil Defense Administration and  \nshall remain under the jurisdiction of  \nthe Federal Civil Defense Administrator  \nuntil further order of the President."
    },
    {
      "char_end": 2014,
      "char_start": 1305,
      "id": "CLAUSES:EO:10222#2",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "2.",
      "pdf_page": 1,
      "scope_id": "EO:10222#2",
      "source": {
        "filing_date": null,
        "location_confidence": "high",
        "location_verified": false,
        "page_or_item": "16 FR 2247, PDF pages 1-1",
        "requires_page_check": false,
        "sha256": "580a64b4658ec58cae0e9ea5709b5689dfa01a3c41b3ba168f0a56417d55a169",
        "signing_date": "1951-03-08",
        "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_10222.txt",
        "text_sha256": "5e744fa498f9cde39f8a2e9b0a14f3e330d8dceee4642fa008d63bf3a5ee9aad",
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1951-03-13/pdf/FR-1951-03-13.pdf"
      },
      "text": "2. There shall be transferred to the  \nFederal Civil Defense Administration  \nsuch of the property and records of the  \nNational Security Resources Board as  \nrelate, as determined jointly by the  \nChairman of the National Security Re­\nsources Board and the Federal Civil De­\nfense Administrator, to the functions  \ntransferred by the provisions of para­\ngraph 1  of this order or to other func­\ntions now vested in the Federal Civil  \nDefense Administration, and such of the  \npersonnel of the Health Resources Office \nof the National Security Resources  \nBoard as the said Chairman and Ad­\nministrator shall jointly determine to be  \nengaged primarily in the performance  \nof the said transferred functions."
    },
    {
